// Gap-fill scheduler: automatic driver for the APPROVED in-stock gap-fill
// list only (Jonathan, 2026-11-02). NOT a general backfill, NOT out-of-stock.
//
// Netlify wakes this on its own timer (see netlify.toml:
// [functions."gapfill-scheduler"], every 30 minutes, UTC). Each wake:
//   1. Reads gapfill-auto.json from Blobs store 'xl-arms-catalog'.
//   2. Reads the image manifest (images.json, same store) and measures
//      how many SKUs in the current batch already have photos.
//   3. If the current batch is fully photographed, or it has made no
//      progress across two consecutive triggered runs, or it has been
//      triggered 3 times, it is marked done (remaining SKUs are recorded
//      as no-file candidates in the state, not lost) and the scheduler
//      moves to the next batch in the SAME wake.
//   4. If the last trigger was less than 20 minutes ago, it skips this
//      wake: the previous background run may still be going (cap 15 min),
//      and two image-sync runs must never write the manifest at once.
//   5. Otherwise it fires one batch's image-sync trigger URL and records
//      the trigger time. The background function answers 202 immediately,
//      so this wake finishes in seconds.
//
// Queue order (generated 2026-11-02 from the live gap-fill report):
// in-stock missing-standard SKUs only (2,884; the 8 Vertx test SKUs are
// already photographed and excluded), biggest shard first: s, c, m, b,
// t, a, h, r, g, f, n, w, k, p, o, l, d, u, e, j, z, x, i, q.
// Phase 1: STANDARD photos only, batches of 100 (?no-hi=1, ?skip-done=1).
// Phase 2: HI-RES only, batches of 50 (?hi-only=1; hi-only already
// skips already-done hi). Out-of-stock missing photos (3,068) are NOT
// in this queue — they stay deferred until back in stock.
//
// Pause: set env var GAPFILL_AUTO_PAUSED=1 (then redeploy) and the
// scheduler logs "paused" and triggers nothing. To stop permanently,
// remove the schedule from netlify.toml and redeploy.
//
// Manual triggering while this scheduler runs is NOT safe: a manual
// trigger can overlap a scheduler-triggered run and race on the manifest.
// Let the scheduler own all image-sync triggering until it logs complete.
// If a manual trigger is ever needed, pause the scheduler first and wait
// 20 minutes.

